<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōpĭa</span></b> , ac,
			f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The goddess of abundance</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps.
				2, 4, 46</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bona,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					9, 88</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opulenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 17, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. C. S. 60 al.</span></i>—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An appellation of the town</i> Lugdunum (Lyons), in
			Gaul, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 194</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">2325</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hence, COPIENSIS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 753, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
